Subject: [flux] Do not show Google's AI Mode button in the omnibox

The address bar shipped with an "AI Mode" button and a "Press tab then enter
to ask AI Mode" hint. That is Google Search's assistant, offered from the
address bar of a browser that has its own agent on Ctrl+K - two assistants
competing for the same gesture, and the one being advertised cannot see a
single thing the user has connected to Flux.

The switch is a real Chromium pref rather than a feature flag, so this only
changes its default. Someone who wants Google's AI mode can still turn it
back on.

--- a/components/omnibox/browser/omnibox_prefs.cc
+++ b/components/omnibox/browser/omnibox_prefs.cc
@@ -26,8 +26,16 @@
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
       kShowGoogleLensShortcut, true,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
+  // Off in Flux. The button is Google Search's AI entry point, sitting in the
+  // address bar of a browser whose own agent is one keystroke away on Ctrl+K -
+  // two assistants competing for the same gesture, one of which is not ours
+  // and cannot see anything the user has connected.
+  //
+  // Left as a pref the user can turn back on rather than compiled out: it is
+  // a real Chromium setting, and someone who wants Google's AI mode should be
+  // able to have it.
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
-      kShowAiModeOmniboxButton, true,
+      kShowAiModeOmniboxButton, false,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
       kShowSearchTools, true, user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
